The '''tenth series''' of ''[[The Great British Bake Off]]'' began on 27 August 2019.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.radiotimes.com/news/tv/2019-08-17/bake-off-2019-start-applications-contestants-filming/|title=When does The Great British Bake Off 2019 start? Who are the contestants? Is there a trailer?|website=[[Radio Times]]|date=17 August 2019}}</ref> It was presented by returning hosts [[Noel Fielding]] and [[Sandi Toksvig]], and judged by returning judges [[Paul Hollywood]] and [[Prue Leith]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.mirror.co.uk/3am/tv-film-news/great-british-bake-offs-paul-18949828|title=Bake Off's Paul Hollywood and Prue Leith on what series 10 has in store|first=Nicola|last=Methven|date=16 August 2019|website=[[Daily Mirror]]}}</ref>

The series was won by [[David Atherton (baker)|David Atherton]], who became the first winner never to have won the Star Baker title since it was introduced. Alice Fevronia and Steph Blackwell finished as runners-up.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/live/2019/oct/29/the-great-british-bake-off-2019-final-live |title =The Great British Bake Off 2019: final – as it happened|date=29 October 2019|work=Guardian|accessdate=30 October 2019}}</ref> This series started with 13 bakers instead of the usual 12, which meant one episode featured a double elimination, as was previously done in the [[The Great British Bake Off (series 4)|fourth series]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.goodhousekeeping.com/uk/lifestyle/a28839623/bake-off-13-bakers-double-elimination/ |title=The Great British Bake Off announces big twist in first episode|first= Megan |last= Sutton|date=28 August 2019|work=Good Housekeeping }}</ref>

