== Specials ==
Two festive specials were commissioned during Christmas Day and New Year’s Day.

=== ''The Great Christmas Bake Off'' ===
The Great Christmas Bake Off featured Briony Williams and Terry Hartill from [[The Great British Bake Off (series 9)|Series 9]], along with Tom Hetherington and Yan Tsou from [[The Great British Bake Off (series 8)|Series 8]]. The special was won by Briony Williams.<ref>{{cite web| url=https://metro.co.uk/2019/12/25/great-british-bake-off-star-briony-williams-hand-christmas-special-2019-11960002/| title=The Great British Bake Off winner Briony Williams triumphs in tent a year on for the Christmas special| first=Sarah| last=Deen| date=25 December 2019| website=metro.co.uk}}</ref>

In the signature challenge, the returning bakers were first asked to make 24 festive [[cake pops]] in {{frac|2|1|2}} hours. They then faced the technical challenge set by Paul, where they had to recreate a festive [[sausage roll]] wreath in 2 hours. For the festive showstopper challenge, the bakers were given the task of constructing a 3D gingerbread building, topped off with at least two different types of confectionery, in 4 hours.
